WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Welcome to week six module one.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.440
Now this module covers vertical expansion.

3
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.360
So basically now that you have your first client,

4
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.000
how do you go deeper with the clients that you already have

5
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.840
and how do you start attracting more?

6
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.040
And in this lesson, we'll cover upsells, addons,

7
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.720
as well as retainers.

8
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.880
Now, if you were due to this,

9
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.720
your instinct may be that once you get your first client

10
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.680
and you want to grow,

11
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.200
the first thought that you may have is to find more clients.

12
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.000
So to expand from client X to client Y and also client Z.

13
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:26.840
But in the real world,

14
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.640
one of the smarter moves that you can do

15
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.800
is to go deeper with the clients that you already serve.

16
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.080
And there's basically three reasons why this works

17
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.320
and why this is important.

18
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.320
The first one is that they already trust you.

19
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.960
So you've already delivered the work,

20
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.560
they already know that you're legitimate

21
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.040
and they already have background in your practice.

22
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.680
The second is that you already understand their business.

23
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.200
So you've been in their world

24
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.880
and you know what matters to them, right?

25
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.440
And sometimes even more importantly,

26
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.480
there is already a working relationship,

27
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.880
which is all of those undefinable characteristics,

28
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.800
which basically lets you work better with them

29
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.200
because you've already talked to them in several meetings

30
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.480
and you know exactly what they place importance in

31
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.480
in your conversations and in the projects

32
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.600
that you are delivering.

33
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.080
And finally, and most importantly,

34
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.680
is that there's no sales cycle

35
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.960
or at least a sales cycle is a bit more shrunk.

36
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.960
So if you remember our dots framework

37
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.360
where you do the discovery and then you do an offer

38
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.560
and then you do a tailoring

39
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.520
and then you seal the deal and contract with them,

40
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.640
that can actually be compressed pretty well.

41
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.400
And if you're already working with them.

42
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.960
In fact, for most of our clients

43
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.120
where we expanded within their services,

44
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.800
obviously there's no cold outreach anymore.

45
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.280
And sometimes there's not even a pitch deck.

46
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.640
It's just a conversation of what else we can offer them

47
00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.000
beyond what we already did.

48
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.440
So to give one example,

49
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.080
we used to develop digital apps

50
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.640
for several clients here in Sydney.

51
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.880
And one of them is this way finding app called PAM in Australia.

52
00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.680
So basically what they do is develop applications for places.

53
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.520
So whenever you go to the mall, for example,

54
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.520
and there's like a map there

55
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.840
that lets customers find their way around things,

56
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.080
technologies like PAM is one of them.

57
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.680
And to give an example of expanding within a client,

58
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.000
apart from developing their digital products,

59
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.080
we also realized that they were looking to actually find leads

60
00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.000
that they can offer their technologies to.

61
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.200
And so what we did is we basically expanded our offering to them

62
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.000
and also offer creative assets to them.

63
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.760
And the reason why it worked is because it's so much easier.

64
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.960
Since we already had the trust,

65
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.680
we already knew their business and we could just ask, right?

66
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.400
Because if you already have that trust with that same client

67
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.040
and you can pinpoint a specific problem that they would have,

68
00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.280
then you might want to start with offering that first

69
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.000
before trying to expand outward

70
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.440
with securing and building new relationships with new clients.

71
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.360
And so how do you do this?

72
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.160
Basically, you just need to look for adjacent problems.

73
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.120
To give an example, let's say you built an agent

74
00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.280
or an automation that finds and contacts leads for a client,

75
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.440
then you can ask, can we also automate the follow up

76
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.280
of this agent?

77
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.640
Let's say you're offering creative and content services.

78
00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.240
If you are successful on YouTube,

79
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.120
then it might be good to now explore other platforms.

80
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.920
So if your content automation is working for YouTube shorts,

81
00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.160
then you can upsell towards also taking care

82
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.440
of their TikTok or their Instagram accounts as well.

83
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.720
And in terms of time savings,

84
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.520
let's say you're saving time on this particular project,

85
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.640
throughout the process of identifying

86
00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.000
and streamlining operations,

87
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.640
for sure, you will identify areas in their business

88
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.640
where time is also being wasted.

89
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.000
And so that's an opportunity for an upsell.

90
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.720
So basically the pattern is look for adjacent problems

91
00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.680
that you can solve.

92
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.160
And the great thing is with the technology that we have now,

93
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.720
if you just open up, let's say, cloud code or anti-gravity

94
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.080
or whatever agent platform that you use in the future,

95
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.800
if you just provide a brief and a well-constructed background

96
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.200
of what it is that you want to help your client on,

97
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.520
often that gives you signals of the right solution

98
00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.160
for that particular issue.

99
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.880
Now, let's talk about retainers for a sec,

100
00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.240
which is basically the part where you charge an ongoing amount

101
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.280
with a client in exchange for a service.

102
00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.560
And there's basically three forms of services

103
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.880
that you may be interested in,

104
00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.680
depending on the model that you are working with

105
00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.520
with your client.

106
00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.360
The first one is a maintenance retainer.

107
00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.840
So this is basically a monthly fee

108
00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:42.960
to maintain what you build.

109
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.360
Updates, fixes, monitoring, for example,

110
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.280
would be falling into this category.

111
00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.400
You can also charge for growth retainers.

112
00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.880
So basically, these are monthly budgets

113
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.080
for ongoing improvements in new features.

114
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.120
So let's say that example we gave earlier

115
00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.680
of expanding from YouTube and then into TikTok

116
00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.080
and Instagram for your client,

117
00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.120
and that is a key example of growth.

118
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.240
And lastly, is your advisory retainer.

119
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.960
So these are regular calls to advice on the AI strategy.

120
00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.680
And this is very important in our field

121
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.600
because remember, a lot of business owners,

122
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.400
they don't have the same time as you

123
00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.200
to become an expert on all the latest AI tools.

124
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.560
In fact, there are people who would pay experts

125
00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.200
in the field a monthly fee or monthly retainer,

126
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.000
just so that they can prepare some sort of presentation to them.

127
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.400
On what specific tools and opportunities

128
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.720
they can use with today's AI tools

129
00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.200
to help with their business.

130
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.680
And this is very common, especially in corporate environments.

131
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.560
Like if you think about the end of the spectrum here,

132
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.680
like the McKinsey's or the BCGs of the world,

133
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.400
literally people pay them millions

134
00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.400
for essentially PowerPoint presentations

135
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.680
that is seeding ideas to their top leadership

136
00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.400
of how let's say they can use AI

137
00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.960
or AI agents in their business.

138
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.320
It's obviously well researched,

139
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.760
but the reason why it's so valuable

140
00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.600
is because you have a high status agency

141
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.480
which is McKinsey, delivering ideas and opportunities

142
00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.240
to a leaders of an organization.

143
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.400
And if that single meeting

144
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.160
and that single PowerPoint presentation

145
00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.440
gives like a 5% incremental to like a billion dollar business,

146
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.760
then you can see where the ROY can come from.

147
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.000
And so if you scale that down

148
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.920
depending on where you are on your journey,

149
00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.000
you can think of that as well.

150
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.320
There is value in delivering ideas to customers, to clients

151
00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.080
and giving out that knowledge of what you know

152
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.840
and the time it took you to understand all of these AI tools

153
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.720
that you spent so much time building up

154
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.920
the technical skills for.

155
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.760
And transmitting them into a jargon

156
00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.360
that business owners understand

157
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.440
because if that helps them save time or make more money,

158
00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.720
then that is very valuable to them

159
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.120
that you can charge for for sure.

160
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.160
And so that's the key message for this module.

161
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.640
You need to go vertical first

162
00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.360
before expanding horizontally.

163
00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.840
You need to think about expanding with your existing clients

164
00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.240
and offer them new services,

165
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.040
become a better steward for their business

166
00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.680
before chasing new ones.

167
00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.520
But for the next module, we'll be talking about referrals,

168
00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.840
which is going to be one of your highest converting source

169
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.760
for new clients.
